HOW TO USE SCITEX:

Requirements:
Linux, Java 11

Setup:
1. Put the scitex directory in a directory (e.g., xml_converter)
2. Modification in main.py in scitex:
	a. Change the jar file name from "grobid-core-0.7.2-SNAPSHOT-onejar.jar" to "grobid-core-0.7.2-onejar.jar"
	b. Set INPUT = "scitex/scitexIn"
	c. Set OUTPUT = "scitex/scitexOut/"
3. Download grobid version 0.7.2 from: https://github.com/kermitt2/grobid
4. Unzip grobid in the same directory as scitex (e.g., xml_converter). Rename the unzipped directory to "grobid".
5. Make sure the scitex and grobid are in the same parent directory (e.g., xml_converter)
6. Go to grobid directory from terminal and execute ./gradlew clean install (this step requires Java 11)

Run Converter:
1. Take whatever PDFs you want to convert and put them into the scitex/scitexIn directory
2. To run the program, execute from the parent directory using the terminal: python3 scitex/main.py
3. The output should be .tei.xml files present in scitex/scitexOut


HOW TO READ THE CODE:
main.py runs grobid on the input folder, then runs pdfalto on each pdf in the input folder, then runs scitex on the grobid and pdfalto outputs.
grobidAltoStuff/scitex.py is the file that contains the main scitex functions.
